--TEST--
A `covariant` parameter is tested when the method is entered, before the body runs, and a value of the wider type throws a `LogicError` that names the method, the parameter, the type and what the value is — through a parent, a grandchild, an interface, a static method, `compareTo`, an `inout` and a variadic parameter, and a callable of the method — `rule:classes/a-covariant-type-is-checked-where-a-value-enters`
--FILE--
<?nvs
class Animal {}
class Dog extends Animal {}
class Cat extends Animal {}
class Puppy extends Dog {}

class Kennel {
    public function feed(Animal $a): string { return "kennel"; }
    public function label(int|string $id): string { return "kennel " . $id; }
    public function walk(?Animal $a): string { return "kennel walk"; }
    public function all(Animal ...$all): uint { return Core\Arr::count($all); }
    public function swap(inout Animal $a): void {}
    public static function adopt(Animal $a): string { return "kennel adopt"; }
    public static function welcome(Animal $a): string { return static::adopt($a); }
}

class DogKennel extends Kennel {
    public function feed(covariant Dog $a): string { return "dog kennel feeds a dog"; }
    public function label(covariant int $id): string { return "dog " . ($id + 1); }
    public function walk(covariant Dog $a): string { return "walks a dog"; }
    public function all(covariant Dog ...$all): uint { return Core\Arr::count($all); }
    public function swap(inout covariant Dog $a): void { $a = new Puppy(); }
    public static function adopt(covariant Dog $a): string { return "adopts a dog"; }
}

class PuppyKennel extends DogKennel {
    public function feed(covariant Dog $a): string { return "puppy kennel feeds a dog"; }
}

interface Feeds {
    public function give(Animal $a): string;
}

class Bowl implements Feeds {
    public function give(covariant Dog|Cat $a): string { return "the bowl takes it"; }
}

class Price implements Comparable {
    public function constructor(public int $cents) {}
    public function compareTo(self $other): int { return $this->cents <=> $other->cents; }
}

class SalePrice extends Price {
    public function compareTo(covariant SalePrice $other): int { return 0; }
}

// A value of the narrower type runs the override, and `int` reaches the body as an `int`.
Kennel $k = new DogKennel();
echo $k->feed(new Dog()), "\n";
echo $k->label(4), "\n";

// 1. A `Cat` through the parent's type.
try {
    echo $k->feed(new Cat()), "\n";
} catch (LogicError $e) {
    echo "1: ", $e->message, "\n";
}

// 2. A `string` where the override takes `int`.
try {
    echo $k->label("x"), "\n";
} catch (LogicError $e) {
    echo "2: ", $e->message, "\n";
}

// 3. A `null` where the override takes `Dog`.
try {
    echo $k->walk(null), "\n";
} catch (LogicError $e) {
    echo "3: ", $e->message, "\n";
}

// 4. A variadic parameter tests each argument.
echo $k->all(new Dog(), new Puppy()), "\n";
try {
    echo $k->all(new Dog(), new Cat()), "\n";
} catch (LogicError $e) {
    echo "4: ", $e->message, "\n";
}

// 5. An `inout` parameter tests the variable on entry, and the body may write a narrower value.
Animal $pet = new Dog();
$k->swap(inout $pet);
echo $pet is Puppy ? "a puppy" : "not a puppy", "\n";
Animal $other = new Cat();
try {
    $k->swap(inout $other);
} catch (LogicError $e) {
    echo "5: ", $e->message, "\n";
}

// 6. A static method, called through `static::` in the parent.
echo DogKennel::welcome(new Dog()), "\n";
try {
    echo DogKennel::welcome(new Cat()), "\n";
} catch (LogicError $e) {
    echo "6: ", $e->message, "\n";
}

// 7. A grandchild.
Kennel $p = new PuppyKennel();
try {
    echo $p->feed(new Cat()), "\n";
} catch (LogicError $e) {
    echo "7: ", $e->message, "\n";
}

// 8. An interface, with `Dog|Cat` where the interface takes `Animal`.
Feeds $bowl = new Bowl();
echo $bowl->give(new Cat()), "\n";
try {
    echo $bowl->give(new Animal()), "\n";
} catch (LogicError $e) {
    echo "8: ", $e->message, "\n";
}

// 9. A callable of the method.
callable $feed = $k->feed(...);
try {
    echo $feed(new Cat()), "\n";
} catch (LogicError $e) {
    echo "9: ", $e->message, "\n";
}

// 10. `compareTo` called directly through the parent.
Price $sale = new SalePrice(5);
try {
    echo $sale->compareTo(new Price(5)), "\n";
} catch (LogicError $e) {
    echo "10: ", $e->message, "\n";
}
// covers: lang:classes/covariant
--EXPECT--
dog kennel feeds a dog
dog 5
1: The parameter `$a` of `DogKennel::feed` has the type `Dog`. The argument is an object of class `Cat`.
2: The parameter `$id` of `DogKennel::label` has the type `int`. The argument is a value of type `string`.
3: The parameter `$a` of `DogKennel::walk` has the type `Dog`. The argument is `null`.
2
4: The parameter `$all` of `DogKennel::all` has the type `Dog`. One of the arguments is an object of class `Cat`.
a puppy
5: The parameter `$a` of `DogKennel::swap` has the type `Dog`. The variable passed is an object of class `Cat`.
adopts a dog
6: The parameter `$a` of `DogKennel::adopt` has the type `Dog`. The argument is an object of class `Cat`.
7: The parameter `$a` of `PuppyKennel::feed` has the type `Dog`. The argument is an object of class `Cat`.
the bowl takes it
8: The parameter `$a` of `Bowl::give` has the type `Dog|Cat`. The argument is an object of class `Animal`.
9: The parameter `$a` of `DogKennel::feed` has the type `Dog`. The argument is an object of class `Cat`.
10: The parameter `$other` of `SalePrice::compareTo` has the type `SalePrice`. The argument is an object of class `Price`.
